## 5. Interfaces (implement exactly these)

```python
# app/connectors/base.py
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from datetime import datetime
from typing import Iterable, Protocol, Literal

Kind = Literal["git_github", "git_ado", "git_gitlab", "ado_boards", "jira_cloud"]

@dataclass
class Health:
    ok: bool
    message: str                      # human readable, e.g. "PAT missing scope vso.work_write"
    checked_at: datetime

@dataclass
class ExternalItem:                   # something we pulled from Jira/ADO
    system: str                       # "jira_cloud" | "ado_boards"
    external_id: str                  # "PROJ-123" | "4512"
    type: str                         # normalized: epic | feature | story | bug | task
    title: str
    description_text: str             # plain text (convert ADF / HTML)
    status: str                       # normalized: todo | in_progress | done
    updated_at: datetime
    url: str
    labels: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    links: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)   # {rel, external_id}
    raw: dict = field(default_factory=dict)           # original payload (stored, not logged)

@dataclass
class OutboundItem:                   # something we push
    codegenome_id: str                # e.g. "wave:1", "module:ledger-data-model"
    type: str                         # epic | feature | story
    title: str
    description_md: str
    acceptance_criteria: list[str]    # one line per recovered rule, with rule id
    parent_codegenome_id: str | None
    labels: list[str]

@dataclass
class PushResult:
    codegenome_id: str
    action: Literal["created", "updated", "unchanged", "skipped_dry_run", "failed"]
    external_id: str | None
    url: str | None
    detail: str = ""

class WorkItemConnector(Protocol):
    kind: Kind
    def test_connection(self) -> Health: ...
    def pull_changes(self, since: datetime) -> Iterable[ExternalItem]: ...
    def handle_webhook(self, headers: dict, body: bytes) -> Iterable[ExternalItem]: ...
    def push(self, item: OutboundItem, dry_run: bool = True) -> PushResult: ...

class SourceConnector(Protocol):
    kind: Kind
    def test_connection(self) -> Health: ...
    def fetch_snapshot(self, repo: str, ref: str, dest_dir: str) -> "SnapshotRef": ...
    def handle_webhook(self, headers: dict, body: bytes) -> "PushEvent | None": ...

@dataclass
class SnapshotRef:
    repo: str
    ref: str                          # branch or tag requested
    commit_sha: str                   # resolved commit
    path: str                         # workspace directory on the jobs volume
    content_hash: str                 # sha256 of the file tree

@dataclass
class PushEvent:
    repo: str
    branch: str
    commit_sha: str
```

## 6. Field mappings

### 6.1 What we push (work items out)

| CodeGenome | Jira Cloud | Azure DevOps Boards |
|---|---|---|
| Wave | Epic | Epic |
| Module / build unit | Story (parent = Epic) | Feature (parent = Epic) |
| Business rule | **One acceptance-criteria line** in the Story, not a separate issue | **One line** in `Microsoft.VSTS.Common.AcceptanceCriteria` |
| `codegenome_id` | Label `cg-<id>` + row in `external_link` | Tag `cg:<id>` in `System.Tags` + row in `external_link` |
| Title | `summary` | `System.Title` |
| Description (Markdown) | `description` as **ADF** (convert from Markdown) | `System.Description` as **HTML** (convert from Markdown) |
| Parent | `parent: {key}` | Relation `System.LinkTypes.Hierarchy-Reverse` |

> Rules become acceptance-criteria lines, not tickets. 800 rules must not create 800 issues.

### 6.2 What we pull (work items in)

| Normalized field | Jira Cloud | Azure DevOps Boards |
|---|---|---|
| `external_id` | `key` | `id` |
| `type` | `issuetype.name` → epic/story/bug/task | `System.WorkItemType` → epic/feature/story/bug/task |
| `status` | `status.statusCategory.key` (new/indeterminate/done) | `System.State` mapped per process template |
| `updated_at` | `fields.updated` | `System.ChangedDate` |
| `description_text` | ADF → plain text | HTML → plain text |
| `labels` | `labels` | `System.Tags` (split on `;`) |
| `links` | `issuelinks`, `parent` | `relations` |

Pull **bugs and incidents** by default (`type in (bug)`); make the filter configurable per connector (JQL / WIQL).

### 6.3 Git source

| Item | Rule |
|---|---|
| Fetch | `git init` + `git fetch --depth 1 origin <sha-or-ref>` + `git checkout FETCH_HEAD` (no full clone) |
| Auth | Token via `GIT_ASKPASS` or a credential helper; **never** put the token in the URL or logs |
| Output | Same workspace layout the zip upload produces today, so `discovery-360` runs unchanged |
| Record | `commit_sha`, `content_hash`, repo, ref on the codebase/job row |

## 7. Database (additive tables)

```sql
CREATE TABLE connector_config (
  connector_id   VARCHAR(64) PRIMARY KEY,
  project_id     VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,          -- tenant scope
  kind           VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,
  base_url       TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- https://dev.azure.com/org, https://x.atlassian.net
  scope_json     JSON NOT NULL,                 -- project key / area path / repo / JQL / WIQL filter
  secret_ref     VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,         -- name of the secret, NOT the secret
  webhook_secret_ref VARCHAR(255),
  enabled        BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
  created_by     VARCHAR(64), created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

CREATE TABLE external_link (                    -- idempotency + traceability
  codegenome_id  VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  connector_id   VARCHAR(64)  NOT NULL,
  external_id    VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL,
  url            TEXT,
  payload_hash   CHAR(64),                      -- skip update if unchanged
  updated_at     TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  PRIMARY KEY (codegenome_id, connector_id),
  UNIQUE KEY (connector_id, external_id)
);

CREATE TABLE external_item (                    -- pulled tickets (defects etc.)
  connector_id   VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,
  external_id    VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL,
  type VARCHAR(32), status VARCHAR(32), title TEXT, description_text LONGTEXT,
  url TEXT, labels_json JSON, links_json JSON, raw_json LONGTEXT,
  updated_at     TIMESTAMP,
  PRIMARY KEY (connector_id, external_id)
);

CREATE TABLE connector_sync_state (             -- feeds Platform health
  connector_id   VARCHAR(64) PRIMARY KEY,
  cursor_at      TIMESTAMP NULL,                -- last successful "since"
  last_success_at TIMESTAMP NULL,
  last_error_at  TIMESTAMP NULL,
  last_error     TEXT,
  errors_24h     INT DEFAULT 0,
  backlog        INT DEFAULT 0
);

CREATE TABLE connector_audit (                  -- every outbound write
  audit_id       VARCHAR(64) PRIMARY KEY,
  connector_id   VARCHAR(64), codegenome_id VARCHAR(255), external_id VARCHAR(128),
  action         VARCHAR(32), dry_run BOOLEAN, payload_hash CHAR(64),
  actor          VARCHAR(64),                   -- user or "system"
  approved_by    VARCHAR(64),                   -- HITL approver for agent-proposed writes
  at             TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
```

## 8. API routes to add

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/connectors` | Create connector config (admin only) |
| GET | `/connectors?project_id=` | List connectors for a project |
| POST | `/connectors/{id}/test` | Run `test_connection`, return `Health` |
| GET | `/connectors/{id}/health` | Values from `connector_sync_state` |
| POST | `/connectors/{id}/pull` | Trigger `pull_changes` now |
| POST | `/connectors/{id}/push?dry_run=true` | Push a plan (body: list of `OutboundItem`), returns `PushResult[]` |
| POST | `/connectors/{id}/replay?since=` | Re-pull from a timestamp |
| POST | `/webhooks/{kind}/{connector_id}` | Inbound webhook (no JWT; signature-verified) |
| POST | `/codebases/from-repo` | Create codebase + start discovery from `{connector_id, repo, ref}` |

All routes except webhooks use the existing JWT auth and must check the caller has access to the project.

## 9. Guardrails (non-negotiable)

1. **Idempotent push.** Look up `external_link` first. If found and `payload_hash` unchanged → `unchanged`. If found → update. If not found → search by label/tag `cg:<id>` (recovers from a lost DB row) → create only if still not found.
2. **`dry_run=True` is the default** everywhere. A real push requires an explicit `dry_run=false`.
3. **Never delete** anything in an external system. No delete code paths.
4. **Secrets by reference only.** `secret_ref` points to an env var / K8s secret / cloud key vault entry. Never store, return or log the value. Redact `Authorization` headers in all logs.
5. **Least privilege.** Document the minimum scopes per connector (e.g. ADO PAT: Work Items Read & Write, Code Read; Jira: read/write issues in the configured project only).
6. **Tenant scope.** Every query filters by the connector's project/scope. A connector must never read another project's items.
7. **Rate limits.** Retry 429 and 5xx with exponential backoff + jitter (max 5 tries), honour `Retry-After`. Respect page sizes (ADO: max 200 ids per batch get; Jira: paginate search).
8. **Webhook security.** Verify signatures where the system supports it (GitHub `X-Hub-Signature-256` HMAC, GitLab `X-Gitlab-Token`). For systems without signing, use a per-connector secret in the webhook URL **plus** basic auth, and reject everything else. Webhook handlers must return fast (enqueue, then process).
9. **Cursor safety.** Store `cursor_at` only after a page is fully processed; overlap the next `since` by 2 minutes and de-duplicate by `(connector_id, external_id, updated_at)`. All times in UTC.
10. **Audit every write** (real or dry-run) in `connector_audit`.


